:"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"dedf57673f50922b0a2d78cfd20e2c1af205da2679e130f066670bb24c9d9ba3","event_uuid":"1363b1aa-02f0-4ec5-9264-dd46611b6f59","position":{"commit_sha":"ba6903d6a144cf608d2539c64e6dbdc6e6dd366d","position":"1787381142933112001-1363b1aa-02f0-4ec5-9264-dd46611b6f59"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fb9c218a9bf2136fced69ad68a6a403871a49959ab4f8af81108ed18189c5ab0","event_uuid":"6a734fe1-91c8-4eb4-8285-561133ebeae1","position":{"commit_sha":"7d782740bc5f8b609398f3160ed46589b2c8761f","position":"1787381151728892001-6a734fe1-91c8-4eb4-8285-561133ebeae1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"FORCE_CLOSE: close gate(s) bypassed by user approval — no completion/signature attestation was signed. Reason: \"Change already MERGED to main (commit 64f3b8c480 'Replay recorded hops on illegal Jira transition') with BOTH Gerrit gates green: Verified+1 (CI full suite) and LLM-Review+1. Stale-material is solely from widening file_impact 2->3 to match the merged commit's actual files (dispatch_one.py, transition_replay.py [new], test_transition_replay.py); all 26 oracle tests pass locally. Re-running plan-review on already-landed, gate-approved code is circular. Same disposition as S3.\". Session: 2456ac87e1.","timestamp":1787381151728892001}],"completion_expectation":"force_bypassed","created_at":1787290326333999001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7b5dbb98-9ddb-43a7-94d5-51b7f3a66213","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"438a-e1d9-29d3-4081"},{"link_uuid":"d0b3dd31-dca1-4a5f-92f8-7434f59aa542","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"f1bc-75f6-ed8c-472f"},{"link_uuid":"e16f8a5a-2c4e-455d-af1c-b36667848a7f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6927-2f97-962e-4448"},{"link_uuid":"f274ad9c-8a9f-4a2c-95a6-31827380ec38","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"78f8-10f0-2ae4-450e"},{"link_uuid":"f5c0f0f8-fd3f-468b-ba17-cf649fdda0f7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"75e2-4f98-661e-4330"}],"description":"# S6: Transition replay fallback for invalid direct Jira transitions\n\n## Context / Problem\nA Jira workflow may forbid the DIRECT end-state transition rebar wants (e.g.\n`open -> done` when only `open -> in_progress -> done` is allowed); the outbound sync\nthen fails and the ticket drifts. Status flows `update_one` ->\n`client.update_issue(status=...)` -> `transition_issue_by_name`. Cloud:\n`AcliClient.transition_issue_by_name` (`adapters/jira/acli.py:489`) lists available\ntransitions, POSTs one hop, raises `RuntimeError` when none reach the target\n(`acli.py:536`) or `urllib.error.HTTPError` on a non-2xx POST. DC:\n`JiraDataCenterTransport.transition_issue_by_name` (`adapters/jira_datacenter/\n_issues.py:229`) -> `transition_to_status` -> `resolve_transition`, which raises\n**`ValueError`** when no transition reaches the target (`transitions.py:104`); the\nillegal-from-current-state case is `IllegalTransitionError`, a `ValueError` subclass\ndeliberately NOT an `HTTPError` (`transitions.py:33-36`). The direct path runs ONE hop\nand gives up; `_update_one_scalar_update` (`dispatch_one.py:583`) turns the failure\ninto comment-fallback + drift (`result=None`).\n\nReplay mirrors rebar's REAL recorded status hops to reach the end state via allowed\nintermediate hops. Self-healing (inventing hops rebar never took) is OUT of scope.\n\n## Approach\n1. **Data source — recorded hops (grounded, event-sourced).** Every transition\n   appends an append-only `STATUS` event `<tracker>/<local_id>/<ts>-STATUS.json`,\n   written by `rebar._commands.txn` (`txn.py` ~L330):\n   `data={\"status\":<target>,\"current_status\":<from>,...}`. Files sort by filename =\n   chronological — the ordering `reduce_ticket` replays in (`reducer/_api.py:138`) and\n   `txn._parent_status_uuid` uses (`txn.py:105`). NEW helper\n   `recorded_status_hops(local_id, tracker) -> list[str]` globs `*-STATUS.json`, sorts\n   by filename, returns the ordered `data[\"status\"]` targets FORWARD-mapped local->Jira\n   via `LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` (`value_maps.py:78-86`). The sequence lives entirely in\n   **Jira-name space**, e.g. `[\"To Do\",\"In Progress\",\"Done\"]`.\n\n2. **Ambiguity-free resume — NO inverse map.** `LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA` is NON-INJECTIVE\n   (`value_maps.py:78-86`: `In Progress` <- {in_progress,blocked}; `Done` <-\n   {closed,cancelled,deleted}), so it has no inverse. We NEVER invert it. Read the\n   issue's current status via the existing required member `client.get_issue(remote_id)`,\n   take `fields.status.name` (a Jira NAME), and match it DIRECTLY against the\n   forward-mapped hop list from (1) — all comparison in Jira-name space. Tie-break: on\n   multiple positional matches anchor on the LAST (highest index; Jira is at its\n   most-recently-synced state) and replay the hops AFTER it. No positional match ->\n   abort (see 4). No local status is ever reconstructed from a Jira name.\n\n3. **Replay uses ONLY the existing seam.** No list-available-transitions method exists;\n   the required member is `TicketTransport.transition_issue_by_name(remote_id,\n   target_status)` (`_backend.py:250`). **No new transport method.** Replay calls it\n   once per remaining Jira-name hop, in order; each call re-fetches the now-current\n   per-issue transitions and executes the next legal hop.\n\n4. **Failure mode — grounded, covers BOTH implementors.** The per-transition\n   required-field abort is DROPPED (no field metadata is fetched and the transport has\n   no method for it). Replay aborts if ANY hop raises the UNION of what both named\n   implementors raise: `RuntimeError` (acli, `acli.py:536`), `ValueError` (DC\n   no-transition AND its `IllegalTransitionError` subclass, `transitions.py:33,104`),\n   `urllib.error.HTTPError`/`JiraAPIError`/`BackendHTTPError` (a 400, incl. an\n   un-fillable required field on the POST). On abort it falls through to the EXISTING\n   comment-fallback + drift arm (`dispatch_one.py:622`, `result=None`). No partial hop\n   is retried.\n\n5. **Call-chain threading (explicit).** The replay call site is inside\n   `_update_one_scalar_update` (`dispatch_one.py:583`), invoked by `update_one`\n   (`:413`) at `:470-472`.\n   - `client`: ALREADY the first parameter of both `update_one` and\n     `_update_one_scalar_update` — in scope at the site, no change.\n   - `local_id`: `update_one` holds it as `mutation.get(\"local_id\")` (`mutation` in\n     scope; cf. `:128`, `:470`). `_update_one_scalar_update` does NOT receive it today,\n     so ADD one parameter `local_id: str | None` to `_update_one_scalar_update` and pass\n     `mutation.get(\"local_id\")` from the `:470-472` call. This is the ONLY signature\n     change; the two `update_one` callers (`apply_handlers.py:347`,\n     `apply_outbound.py:161`) are UNTOUCHED — `mutation` already flows into `update_one`.\n   - `tracker` / `repo_root`: NOT threaded. `replay_transition` derives the store via\n     `config.tracker_dir(reconciler_repo_root())` — `reconciler_repo_root()`\n     (`config.py:512`) is the reconciler-owned root this module ALREADY self-resolves\n     (`dispatch_one.py:156-158`, `:275-277`); `config.tracker_dir(root)`\n     (`config.py:135`) applies the store's config precedence. No `repo_root`/`tracker`\n     parameter is added anywhere.\n   Wiring: in the widened failure catch (union in 4), call `replay_transition(client,\n   issue_key, local_id, target_status)` FIRST (it self-resolves the tracker); only if it\n   returns False does the current comment-fallback run. Falsy `local_id` -> skip replay,\n   comment-fallback as today.\n\n## Scope\n- NEW `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/transition_replay.py`:\n  `recorded_status_hops(local_id, tracker)` and `replay_transition(client, remote_id,\n  local_id, target_status)` (resolves the tracker via\n  `config.tracker_dir(reconciler_repo_root())`). Keeps `dispatch_one.py` (**678 LOC**;\n  hard cap 800 — `AGENTS.md` module-size policy) under the cap.\n- EDIT `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py`: (a) add `local_id: str |\n  None` parameter to `_update_one_scalar_update` and pass `mutation.get(\"local_id\")` at\n  the `:470-472` call; (b) widen the except in `_update_one_scalar_update` to the union\n  in (4) and call `replay_transition` before comment-fallback; (c) import the helper. No\n  change to `update_one`'s signature or to its two callers.\n- No transport/protocol change; no new required member.\n\n## Testing\nNEW `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_transition_replay.py`: fake Cloud and DC\ntransports recording `transition_issue_by_name` calls (DC fake raising\n`ValueError`/`IllegalTransitionError`, Cloud fake raising `RuntimeError`), an on-disk\ntracker of `*-STATUS.json` events, and `reconciler_repo_root`/`tracker_dir` pointed at it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `test_replay_walks_recorded_intermediate_hops` — hops open->in_progress->closed,\n  workflow rejecting the direct hop: transport receives `transition_issue_by_name(\n  \"In Progress\")` then `(\"Done\")`, in order.\n- [x] `test_replay_resume_point_matches_in_jira_name_space` — `get_issue` reporting\n  \"In Progress\" replays only \"Done\"; resume index found WITHOUT inverting the map.\n- [x] `test_replay_duplicate_jira_name_anchors_on_last_occurrence` — \"In Progress\" at\n  two positions resumes after the LAST match.\n- [x] `test_replay_never_invents_unrecorded_hops` — a hop absent from the recorded\n  sequence is never sent.\n- [x] `test_replay_aborts_and_drifts_on_illegal_hop` — PARAMETRIZED over BOTH backends:\n  a mid-chain hop raising `RuntimeError` (Cloud) AND one raising\n  `IllegalTransitionError`/`ValueError` (DC) each abort replay and run comment-fallback\n  (`result is None`, no further hops).\n- [x] `test_recorded_status_hops_orders_by_filename` — targets returned in filename\n  order, forward-mapped to Jira names.\n- [x] `test_replay_aborts_when_current_status_not_in_sequence` — a Jira status name\n  absent from the hop list aborts to drift.\n- [x] `test_replay_skipped_when_local_id_absent` — a mutation with no `local_id` skips\n  replay and behaves as today (comment-fallback + drift).\n\nTest tier: unit","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py","reason":"transition replay fallback in illegal-transition branch"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/transition_replay.py","reason":"new transition-replay module (walk recorded hops)"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_transition_replay.py","reason":"transition-replay oracle tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","force_close_reason":"Change already MERGED to main (commit 64f3b8c480 'Replay recorded hops on illegal Jira transition') with BOTH Gerrit gates green: Verified+1 (CI full suite) and LLM-Review+1. Stale-material is solely from widening file_impact 2->3 to match the merged commit's actual files (dispatch_one.py, transition_replay.py [new], test_transition_replay.py); all 26 oracle tests pass locally. Re-running plan-review on already-landed, gate-approved code is circular. Same disposition as S3.","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","438a-e1d9-29d3-4081"],["depends_on","f1bc-75f6-ed8c-472f"],["parent","3d7a-7795-efde-4df7"],["relates_to","6927-2f97-962e-4448"],["relates_to","75e2-4f98-661e-4330"],["relates_to","78f8-10f0-2ae4-450e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","parent_status_uuid":"1363b1aa-02f0-4ec5-9264-dd46611b6f59","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d458-bb1e-cc63-42a6","ticket_type":"story","title":"Transition replay fallback for invalid direct Jira transitions","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d0b3dd31-dca1-4a5f-92f8-7434f59aa542","75d71582-3ef6-4bf8-9280-3b635d3d951e","3d7931c5-dba2-4133-b728-4b62f81989b4","abf43ff1-aedc-4823-9cee-02be82fce423","f9b36a84-949a-450f-b709-e375ba224655","05907e6f-0ebd-4520-b35d-3b6eb9e679aa","0c93f68a-aa7c-4716-bcd4-1a304818a1d7","e16f8a5a-2c4e-455d-af1c-b36667848a7f","f274ad9c-8a9f-4a2c-95a6-31827380ec38","f5c0f0f8-fd3f-468b-ba17-cf649fdda0f7","19d07201-9fb6-45df-b7ea-98055a4ce2e4","db58f43e-2527-43ff-b54b-25df8b24c5f4","1363b1aa-02f0-4ec5-9264-dd46611b6f59","6a734fe1-91c8-4eb4-8285-561133ebeae1"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787384187967391001,"uuid":"c8f5741e-807a-42e4-8926-d8436e86e305"}